{"name":"Salvia","hex":"#a8b59e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Salvia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Lamiaceae – sage plants."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Italian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Salvia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salvia","blocks":[{"text":"Salvia is the largest genus of plants in the sage family Lamiaceae, with just under 1,000 species of shrubs, herbaceous perennials, and annuals. Within the Lamiaceae, Salvia is part of the tribe Mentheae within the subfamily Nepetoideae. One of several genera commonly referred to as sage, it includes two widely used herbs, Salvia officinalis and Salvia rosmarinus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Salvia_officinalis0.jpg/330px-Salvia_officinalis0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salvia","wikidata":"Q157151"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Salvia_tingitana%2C_in_Behbahan.jpg/500px-Salvia_tingitana%2C_in_Behbahan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Salvia_tingitana%2C_in_Behbahan.jpg/1280px-Salvia_tingitana%2C_in_Behbahan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Salvia_tingitana%2C_in_Behbahan.jpg/500px-Salvia_tingitana%2C_in_Behbahan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Salvia tingitana flower in Behbahan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalvia_tingitana%2C_in_Behbahan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Anthophora_on_Salvia_1.jpg/500px-Anthophora_on_Salvia_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https: